{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"Root cause and deterministic reproduction (py3.12 GIL build, mechanism-level; no py3.14t interpreter on this host).\n\nObservation: run 41749721339 `sweep (py3.14t)` fails only this test with \"the bound op-cert key ... does not exist\". Holding the test's worker thread 200 ms between `Thread.start()` and its first line reproduces the identical error on py3.12 every run; the unmodified test passes there.\n\nMechanism: `run_mcp` waits for the in-flight gauge to reach 0 before `mcp_server.main()` deletes the signer's key copy. A drained tool call was only counted once its worker ran `gauge.track` — the first line of the instrumented wrapper. FastMCP hands calls to an AnyIO worker (`_thread_offloaded`), so between the worker picking the call up and that line the gauge read 0. If the transport stopped in that window, `run_mcp` returned, the key copy was deleted, and the close then committed STATUS and failed to sign. The test's fake server had the same gap (bare `threading.Thread`). Free-threaded CPython runs the serving thread in parallel with the worker, which makes the window reachable; the GIL build usually lets the new thread run first. The second ticket hypothesis (another test cleaning `rebar-opcert-*`) is not needed to explain the failure: the key path in the log belongs to this test's own `box_binding`, which this test itself cleans up.\n\nFix (in `src/rebar/_mcp_health.py`): a drained tool is counted on the event loop when it is handed to a worker (`InFlightGauge.admit`, same refusal while draining), and the worker runs the uncounted body. A start/abandon handshake makes exactly one side release the count: the worker when the body ends, or the abandoning caller if the worker had not started — then the body is skipped, as AnyIO already skips a cancelled call. The count stays 1 per call.\n\nTests (fail before, pass after): `test_mcp_tool_offload.py::test_a_drained_call_is_counted_before_its_worker_runs_it`, `test_mcp_drain_signing_iguanodon.py::test_close_picked_up_but_not_started_when_the_server_stops_never_runs`. The existing end-to-end test now runs through the real `wire_health` + AnyIO offload instead of a bare thread."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793762721979025001,"uuid":"e608f7f0-0d19-4bf8-9786-9889db4d3be8"}